          "reasoning_content": "We need to propose source-supported person/organization roles from entries and name candidates.\n\nWe have entries:\n0: \"Dr. Mei-Ling O’Neil spoke with Óscar Núñez at A\u0026B Holdings, Inc. (ABH).\"\nTokens list.\n\nEntry1: \"ABH later thanked O’Neil.\"\n\nNames: n0 = Mei-Ling O’Neil (person, entry0). n1 = Óscar Núñez (person). n2 = A\u0026B Holdings, Inc. (organization). n3 = ABH (organization). n4 = O’Neil (person) entry1 (probably same as n0 but different candidate). Note we cannot merge; they are separate IDs but refer possibly to same person. We must not assume they are same. However we can interpret ambiguous binding.\n\nWe need to identify roles. The statements are about speaking and thanking, not role claims. So no occupational role etc. So likely no role interpretations. Any correction? No.\n\nThus we produce empty selections, interpretations, context_links. But we must return selections array? The spec: Return only selections, interpretations and context_links arrays. So we include empty arrays.\n\nThus output:\n\n{\n \"selections\": [],\n \"interpretations\": [],\n \"context_links\": []\n}\n\nMake sure format is JSON with these keys."
